import{_ as i,C as r,o as s,c as a,al as t,E as n}from"./chunks/framework.CsIJ-TGx.js";const b=JSON.parse('{"title":"","description":"","frontmatter":{"layout":"page"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"cookie-settings.md","filePath":"cookie-settings.md"}'),c={name:"cookie-settings.md"};function d(l,e,h,u,p,f){const o=r("CookieToggles");return s(),a("div",null,[e[0]||(e[0]=t('<h2 id="cookie-notice-for-the-eopf-sentinel-zarr-explorer" tabindex="-1">Cookie Notice for the EOPF Sentinel Zarr Explorer <a class="header-anchor link" href="#cookie-notice-for-the-eopf-sentinel-zarr-explorer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cookie Notice for the EOPF Sentinel Zarr Explorer&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The European Space Agency (herein the “Agency” or “ESA”) is an intergovernmental organisation established by its Convention opened for signature in Paris on 30 May 1975 having its headquarters located at 24 rue du Général Bertrand, CS 45741, 75738 Paris Cedex 15, France. ESA is subject to its Framework on Personal Data Protection: <a href="http://www.esa.int/About_Us/Law_at_ESA/Highlights_of_ESA_rules_and_regulations" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">http://www.esa.int/About_Us/Law_at_ESA/Highlights_of_ESA_rules_and_regulations</a></p><p>This cookie notice applies to the EOPF Sentinel Zarr Explorer website (explorer.eopf.copernicus.eu). The EOPF Sentinel Zarr Explorer is a platform for accessing and visualising Sentinel Earth Observation data, enabling real-time exploration of imagery through the GeoZarr data format.</p><h4 id="about-cookies" tabindex="-1">About cookies <a class="header-anchor link" href="#about-cookies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;About cookies&quot;">​</a></h4><p>A cookie is a small text file that a website may save on your device, for instance a mobile device or computer, upon your visit to the website. Cookies may allow a website to recognise an individual&#39;s device and store some information about the user. A cookie can be classified by its lifespan and the domain to which it belongs. By lifespan, a cookie is either a: (i) session cookie which is erased when the user closes the browser; or (ii) persistent cookie which remains on the user&#39;s computer/device for a pre-defined period of time. As for the domain to which the cookie belongs, there are either:</p><ul><li>first-party cookies which are set by the web server of the visited page and share the same domain;</li><li>third-party cookies stored by a different domain to the visited page&#39;s domain. This can happen when the webpage references a file, such as JavaScript, located outside its domain.</li></ul><p>You may refuse non-essential cookies or withdraw your consent at any time.</p>',7)),n(o),e[1]||(e[1]=t('<h4 id="strictly-necessary-cookies" tabindex="-1">Strictly Necessary Cookies <a class="header-anchor link" href="#strictly-necessary-cookies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Strictly Necessary Cookies&quot;">​</a></h4><p>Strictly necessary cookies are used on this website (explorer.eopf.copernicus.eu). Strictly necessary cookies are processed on the basis of legitimate interest to ensure the proper functioning of the website. Without these cookies you would not be able to access the services or the website, and therefore this category cannot be disabled.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>First/Third Party</th><th>Cookie Name</th><th>Session or Persistent</th><th>Type of personal data collected</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Expires</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>explorer.eopf.copernicus.eu</td><td>First Party</td><td>mtm_consent_removed</td><td>Persistent</td><td>Users&#39; cookies consent response</td><td>Opt-out management</td><td>13 months</td></tr><tr><td>explorer.eopf.copernicus.eu</td><td>First Party</td><td>mtm_consent</td><td>Session</td><td>Users&#39; cookies consent response</td><td>Consent management</td><td>13 months</td></tr></tbody></table><h4 id="analytics-cookies" tabindex="-1">Analytics Cookies <a class="header-anchor link" href="#analytics-cookies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Analytics Cookies&quot;">​</a></h4><p>Analytics cookies are used for the purpose of improving the EOPF Sentinel Zarr Explorer service. These cookies collect anonymous data (an individual cannot be identified) about user interaction with this website and is accessible to ESA workforce and the consortium involved in the specific activity. Analytics cookies can be rejected by selecting &quot;Reject all&quot; when you first access the website.</p><p>This website uses the open-source software <strong>Matomo</strong>. Matomo uses cookies to help the website analyse how users use the site. The information generated by the cookie about your use of our website (including your IP address and the URLs of the accessed pages) will be stored and will not be disclosed to third parties. Your IP address is made anonymous by truncating it.</p><p>Personal data collected through cookies is processed solely for the purposes described in this notice and is not used for any incompatible purposes. We will use this information for the purpose of evaluating your use of our website, compiling reports on website activity, and providing other services relating to website activity and internet usage. We will not associate your IP address with any other data held by us.</p><p>Our processing using the Matomo software is based on your consent. This consent can be withdrawn at any time with effect for the future. You may also refuse the use of cookies by selecting the appropriate settings on your browser. However, please note that if you do this, you may not be able to use the full functionality of this website.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>First/Third Party</th><th>Cookie Name</th><th>Session or Persistent</th><th>Type of personal data collected</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Expires</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>explorer.eopf.copernicus.eu</td><td>First Party</td><td>_pk_id</td><td>Persistent</td><td>Anonymized user id</td><td>Track user</td><td>13 months</td></tr><tr><td>explorer.eopf.copernicus.eu</td><td>First Party</td><td>_pk_ses</td><td>Session</td><td>Anonymized user session</td><td>Track session</td><td>30 mins</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The Matomo solution is hosted on EOX IT Services GmbH dedicated servers in <a href="https://faster.cz" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Faster</a> data centre in Brno, Czech Republic. The raw data is retained for a maximum period of 25 months from the date of collection and shall be deleted afterwards.</p><h4 id="third-party-cookies" tabindex="-1">Third-party Cookies <a class="header-anchor link" href="#third-party-cookies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Third-party Cookies&quot;">​</a></h4><p>Various EOPF Sentinel Zarr Explorer webpages link to or show the content of external providers such as Discourse, GitHub, ESA or Copernicus websites, and EOPF websites. If you access such third-party content, the specific conditions, terms, and the cookie policies of these third parties apply. ESA has no control over these, therefore please refer to their separate conditions prior to accepting these. If you do not view third-party content, third-party cookies are not installed on your device.</p><h4 id="how-to-withdraw-your-consent-and-or-delete-a-cookie" tabindex="-1">How to withdraw your consent and/or delete a cookie? <a class="header-anchor link" href="#how-to-withdraw-your-consent-and-or-delete-a-cookie" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How to withdraw your consent and/or delete a cookie?&quot;">​</a></h4><p><strong>Cookie Preferences</strong>: You can withdraw your consent for each cookie category (except strictly necessary cookies) at any time by selecting your preferences in the &quot;Cookie Preferences&quot; panel. By revoking your consent, the cookies therein described will be deleted.</p><p><strong>Using Your Browser</strong>: All the cookies used on our website can be disabled through your browser. To disable cookies through your browser, follow your browser instructions (e.g. within the &quot;Help&quot;, &quot;Tools&quot;, or &quot;Edit&quot; menus in your browser). Please note that blocking or deleting cookies may lead to reduced functionality of some features on the website.</p><h4 id="contact" tabindex="-1">Contact <a class="header-anchor link" href="#contact" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Contact&quot;">​</a></h4><p>If you would like to exercise your rights under Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, or if you have comments, questions or concerns, or if you would like to submit a complaint regarding the collection and use of your personal data, please feel free to contact the ESA Data Protection Officer: Email: <a href="mailto:DPO@ESA.int" class="link" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">DPO@ESA.int</a></p><div class="large-space"></div>',18))])}const k=i(c,[["render",d]]);export{b as __pageData,k as default};
